 "$comment": "The Universal Wallet's declarations (lib/wallet.js), all on the kernel. A wallet DEFINITION is a node of the definition kind, placed in the definitions hierarchy under the definition it refines — to any depth — and every setting (the value classes it may hold, the operations it allows, its policy) is a kernel setting assigned at a definition node and resolved by context: from a wallet up through its definitions, the store's namespace before the platform's, at any moment and as believed at any moment. A definition declares only what differs from the one above it. A WALLET is a node of the wallet kind in its store's namespace, placed under its definition and under its holder; its name, aliases, unit and status are attributes with valid and recorded time, its holder's identity is sealed (a sensitive attribute) and found by a blind index. Value moves only as balanced, immutable journals, each an event in the kernel's hash-chained log; the ledger tables are their index, verified against the log.",
